{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415905-pantheons-of-cultures-that-don-t-exist-yet","id":1415905,"title":"Pantheons of cultures that don't exist yet.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-28T17:21:46-07:00","id":1415905,"title":"Pantheons of cultures that don't exist yet.","content":"My understanding and I am sure god will go into much better detail is once a group is written into the World it can be said to be retconned in. So could we see gods who's cultures don't exist yet manifesting working to make sure their would be followers exist..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T17:32:14-07:00","id":1415906,"title":"","content":"I think a big part of the god book will go into creation myths and how to make your own.<br /> The specifics of which will only be known when the actual book is out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T18:27:43-07:00","id":1415916,"title":"","content":"It would make a grand adventure to have a Moon God manipulating governments to promote space colonization. Both because they want cities on the moon and because they want their scions to become the patrons of new peoples.<br /> <br /> It could also be useful for players that see a major nation, like the USA and Canada, that lack their own pantheons, who want to become those pantheons. It could also detail the possible moves and actions of those that don't want those places to have pantheons. I could see many reasons why a Native American pantheon, that wasn't hostile to the USA, might want to prevent the existence of an American Pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T19:57:57-07:00","id":1415928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1415905-pantheons-of-cultures-that-don-t-exist-yet?p=1415916#post1415916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could also be useful for players that see a major nation, like the USA and Canada, that lack their own pantheons, who want to become those pantheons. It could also detail the possible moves and actions of those that don't want those places to have pantheons. I could see many reasons why a Native American pantheon, that wasn't hostile to the USA, might want to prevent the existence of an American Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the USA and Canada have a LOT of Pantheons. Like, SO many. And I'm not even talking about First Nations (of which I'm sure there are many in Scion that won't get official writeups due to many of the surviving not wanting to talk to Scion's writers, just, hundreds or thousands of Gods and Pantheons of the people of North America), there's people in America who worship all kinds of Gods, and their beliefs are as valid as the worshippers in the other countries. In the World there would be so many Pantheons who have influence in the US. There are churches and sacred sites. I mentioned in another thread, things like &quot;There are like 11 shinto shrines in America, those count as sacred&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus there are Gods who originate IN America: Even if Columbia's writeup from the Companion got removed for reconsideration, she exists. Heck, one of those Shrines I mentioned? One of them is the Daijingu Shrine in Honolulu, and one of the Kami enshrined there is Washington-no-Kami. Yeah, George Washington is deified as a Kami, among others. Give <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/312878/Mantles-of-Washington\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> a look if you'd like to know more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T11:59:22-07:00","id":1416015,"title":"","content":"As far as the other part of the topic goes, whether or not you could have gods running around for a culture that doesn't exist yet because Fate retcons them in when they do, there are two angles that come to my mind aside from the obvious of your table your thing.<br /> <br /> The first is that a God wouldn't exist in the normal world until their people exist even if they've been since the beginning. To explain I'm first gonna say that my grasp on the real world historical timeline is not 100% so just take it as an illustrative hypothetical. So the Anunna and the Teotl both have stories that say those pantheons, their Titans etc, created the world thus we'll assume both Pantheons and its members have existed since the start of the world. However, let's assume that the Anunna's followers existed in the world proper before the Teotl's followers. While the Babylonians/Mesopotamians were around their gods were in the world and doing their thing. The Teotl by contrast would be in their Terra Incognita going through their origin of the world story until the point where their civilizations would actually emerge into the world proper in which case the Teotl would be there in the appropriate manifestation.<br /> <br /> The other to my mind is just that the Pantheon is retconned in like a comic book retcon. Everyone in universe remembers the thing, and going forward if its that kind of thing there will be evidence of it for however long its been a thing, but they aren't actually in the comic until they're there even if they're retconned in as having existed since the dawn of time. So even if a group went out of their way to say become the Valar and as per their mythology retroactively helped make the world next year, entities aware of Fate altering the world's history (such as the individuals who became the Valar) would also be aware that they were not actually around in the 1930s in doing whatever interactions with Tolkein the rewritten reality has them in now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T13:30:38-07:00","id":1416024,"title":"","content":"I think the Brigitte Fiction casts a slight bit of insight into this.<br /> <br /> Like, Brigitte accomplishes her Deed, and the epilogue notes that nobody's heard from Brigitte de la Croix in a long time. And on a completely unrelated note, here, let's make an offering to this city's protector Loa, Baronne Brigitte.<br /> <br /> Like, at one point, there was always Baronne Brigitte. She was just kinda always there, y'know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}